<xliff xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:2.0" xmlns:swi18n="https://step-wise.com/ns/i18n" version="2.1" srcLang="en" trgLang="de">
	<file id="catalog">
		<group id="meta">
			<unit id="learningGoals">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">This skill is about understanding how to <pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">multiply and divide fractions</pc>. This includes various situations.<pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:list" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:a" swi18n:slot="children">Multiplying a number by a fraction: <ph id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c7" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c8" type="ui" subType="swi18n:b" swi18n:slot="children">Multiplying two fractions: <ph id="c9" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c10" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c11" type="ui" subType="swi18n:c" swi18n:slot="children">Dividing a number by fraction: <ph id="c12" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c13" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c14" type="ui" subType="swi18n:d" swi18n:slot="children">Dividing a fraction by a number: <ph id="c15" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c16" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c17" type="ui" subType="swi18n:e" swi18n:slot="children">Dividing a fraction by a fraction: <ph id="c18" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc></pc>Any multiplication/division of fractions should be reduced to a single fraction, where the key is that each factor appears on the correct side of this fraction. Further simplifications are not required.</pc></source>
					<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="87e95b70a31a208b" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="62ff39c215eaf61b"><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Bei dieser Kompetenz geht es darum zu verstehen, wie man <pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">Brüche multipliziert und dividiert</pc>. Dazu gehören mehrere Situationen.<pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:list" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:a" swi18n:slot="children">Multiplikation einer Zahl mit einem Bruch: <ph id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c7" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c8" type="ui" subType="swi18n:b" swi18n:slot="children">Multiplikation zweier Brüche: <ph id="c9" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c10" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c11" type="ui" subType="swi18n:c" swi18n:slot="children">Dividieren einer Zahl durch einen Bruch: <ph id="c12" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c13" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c14" type="ui" subType="swi18n:d" swi18n:slot="children">Dividieren eines Bruchs durch eine Zahl: <ph id="c15" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c16" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c17" type="ui" subType="swi18n:e" swi18n:slot="children">Dividieren eines Bruchs durch einen Bruch: <ph id="c18" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc></pc>Jede Multiplikation/Division von Brüchen sollte auf einen einzigen Bruch reduziert werden, wobei es darauf ankommt, dass jeder Faktor auf der richtigen Seite dieses Bruchs steht. Weitere Vereinfachungen sind nicht erforderlich.</pc></target>
				</segment>
			</unit>
		</group>
	</file>
